      "comment": "Grazina: Mandragora origin",
      "content": "Grazina's kuuvahki-absorbing plant had no name. Brahe, a self-styled master thief, \"stole the naming rights\" and called it Mandragora, after a fictional plant in northern legend. Grazina notes that in the language of flowers it symbolises happiness and hope, and calls it a bitter irony.",
